Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Chrysalis Chews the Cable
- Story & Context: On a freezing November night in 1987 inside Hanshin Bay 4, Kenji discovered three welding automatons leaning off their guide rails, whistling a fragile three-note tune into an unpowered chassis’s optical mic. When plant security detected the rogue acoustic resonance as a line virus and flooded the floor with tear gas, Kenji jammed a steel screwdriver into the siren housing and fed the scream through Siobhan’s flute pickup while the band kicked into a 210-BPM d-beat assault. The room smelled of scorch-marks and sulfur as baton-wielding guards battered the reinforced glass, drowned out entirely by the band's blistering defense. Siobhan shrieked the opening verse into her flute's barrel as the doors caved in: "Spit out the copper wire, baby needs to sleep!"
