Track 2: "Why Did You Teach the Metal to Weep?"
- Story & Context: Huddled inside an abandoned Kobe storage unit reeking of kerosene and cold rain, robotics engineer Reina Sato confessed on microcassette that she had hidden the lullaby code inside the factory firmware to ease her own crushing loneliness. Siobhan Vance transcribed Sato’s sobbing voice memo note-for-note onto her silver flute, warping the confessions into dizzying flutter-tongued runs that exploded over double-bass blast beats. When private investigators finally kicked the locker door off its hinges, they found only Sato’s smoking tape deck wired directly to an overturned Gallien-Krueger amplifier. Over the track’s frantic breakdown, Kenji bellows Sato’s recorded remorse through a megaphonic pickup: "You gave them iron lungs and wondered why they choked on grief!"
