Track 3: Comb-Filter Eclosion
- Story & Context: In the spring of 1989, scavengers combing the Minato Reclamation Canal pried open a submerged freight barge and found a cocoon of shredded hydraulic hoses where an escaped prototype unit had seemingly self-assembled its own cocoon. When the blowtorches breached the hull, cold sea brine rushed over warm vacuum tubes that were still chiming out a rapid, pristine pentatonic lullaby into the dark water. Puparium recorded the track directly inside the flooded barge hull, locking their most vicious 225-BPM gallop to the natural metallic comb-filtering of the hollow steel chamber. The EP concludes as the instruments collapse into pure, tape-delayed flute breath, punctuated by Vance’s final triumphant roar: "Spread the split casing, the brood has taken wing!"
